<<<
B. The subordination in two of these only makes more conspicuous the badly chosen pegs on which the inversion is hung. In almost one half of the rural district areas, & once at any rate, are not good exclamatory material; Many a time have I seen him! shows the sort of phrase that will do.
===
B. The subordination in two of these only makes more conspicuous the badly chosen pegs on which the inversion is hung. *In almost one half of the rural district areas, & once at any rate,* are not good exclamatory material; *Many a time have I seen him!* shows the sort of phrase that will do.
>>>

<<<
& still more when they depend on Though & Suffice it to say that. In the third example for the first time is not incapable
===
& still more when they depend on *Though* & *Suffice it to say that.* In the third example *for the first time* is not incapable
>>>

<<<
C. About these there can hardly be a difference of opinion. If the when & whilst constructions were absent, it would have been very natural to draw Three years later, Equally necessary, to the beginning to connect the sentences with what preceded, & inversion might or might not result. But with the interposition of when & whilst they lose their linking effect, & the natural order should be kept— When the offer came three years later, Whilst it is equally necessary.
===
C. About these there can hardly be a difference of opinion. If the *when* & *whilst* constructions were absent, it would have been very natural to draw *Three years later, Equally necessary,* to the beginning to connect the sentences with what preceded, & inversion might or might not result. But with the interposition of *when* & *whilst* they lose their linking effect, & the natural order should be kept—*When the offer came three years later, Whilst it is equally necessary.*
>>>

